title: PowerShell Spawned by IIS Worker Process - Possible Web Shell Activity
id: 5d8c3b2a-41e7-4f96-b0a5-2c93e7d46b18
status: experimental
description: Detects powershell.exe or pwsh.exe launched as a child of the IIS worker process (w3wp.exe). The Symantec-reported intrusion at a major African stock exchange ran a 41-module credential-harvesting PowerShell toolkit under an IIS web shell, so an interactive interpreter under w3wp.exe is a strong web-shell indicator.
references:
  - https://www.security.com/threat-intelligence/african-stock-exchange-ai-assisted-attack
  - https://therecord.media/witchetty-espionage-group-targeted-two-middle-eastern-govts-stock-exchange-of-african-nation
  - https://gbhackers.com/african-stock-exchange-credential-theft/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/11/23
tags:
  - attack.t1100
  - attack.t1086
  - attack.t1059
  - attack.t1552
logsource:
  category: process_creation
  product: windows
detection:
  selection_parent:
    ParentImage|endswith: '\w3wp.exe'
  selection_interpreter:
    Image|endswith:
      - '\powershell.exe'
      - '\pwsh.exe'
  filter_maintenance:
    ParentCommandLine|contains:
      - 'HealthCheck'
      - 'ConfigurationManager'
    User|endswith:
      - '$'
  condition: selection_parent and selection_interpreter and not filter_maintenance
falsepositives:
  - Application pools hosting legitimate PowerShell automation, CI agents or Exchange/SharePoint maintenance tasks
level: medium
